1c2efa-cbed-55e3-967d-daf6bf46e742" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-bfa28e82-e7a7-5631-a9aa-0b573881c151"] [17592186176088 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7d1c2efa-cbed-55e3-967d-daf6bf46e742"] [17592186176273 :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(T)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}$"] [17592186176273 :question/worked-solution "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have that\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""] [17592186176273 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186173896 :answer-field/correct 17592186173900] ["activity-9ea48e0e-20fc-57ae-8fc6-7c2c77548e20" :activity/id #uuid "9ea48e0e-20fc-57ae-8fc6-7c2c77548e20"] ["step-1855919c-4174-5759-93cf-11a0280966ca" :step/id #uuid "1855919c-4174-5759-93cf-11a0280966ca"] ["step-521a6f9a-99a3-57bc-b710-6c05998470da" :step/id #uuid "521a6f9a-99a3-57bc-b710-6c05998470da"] ["step-cea9ce61-7dee-5a91-9c27-e1a1933f13fb" :step/id #uuid "cea9ce61-7dee-5a91-9c27-e1a1933f13fb"] ["step-af32582e-7c99-52e2-a82b-8a159c337dcb" :step/id #uuid "af32582e-7c99-52e2-a82b-8a159c337dcb"] ["step-33095b71-1333-5602-a459-f3798f52eba0" :step/id #uuid "33095b71-1333-5602-a459-f3798f52eba0"] ["step-1855919c-4174-5759